# Component Architecture Guide

> **Related Rules**: [Frontend Component Patterns](frontend-component-patterns.mdc) | [GraphQL Integration](graphql-integration-patterns.mdc) | [Testing Standards](testing-standards.mdc) | [TableGrid Usage](table-grid-basic-usage.mdc)

## Component Organization Principles

### Directory Structure
```
components/
├── common/                    # Shared, reusable components
│   ├── dialogs/              # Modal and dialog components
│   ├── TableGrid/            # Data table with pagination
│   ├── Button.tsx            # Standard button component
│   ├── UserCard.tsx          # User display component
│   └── Modal.tsx             # Base modal wrapper
├── inputs/                   # Form input components
│   ├── InputField.tsx        # Standard text input
│   ├── DropDownSelector/     # Dropdown with search
│   ├── CreatableTagSelector.tsx # Tag input with creation
│   └── OptimisticDatePicker.tsx # Date picker with optimistic updates
├── layout/                   # Layout and navigation components
│   ├── Page.tsx              # Main page wrapper
│   ├── Header.tsx            # Site header
│   └── Footer.tsx            # Site footer
└── pages/                    # Page-specific components
    ├── CourseContent/        # Feature-oriented organization
    │   ├── Registration/     # Registration feature
    │   │   ├── index.tsx     # Main component
    │   │   ├── types.ts      # Type definitions
    │   │   ├── hooks/        # Feature-specific hooks
    │   │   └── README.md     # Feature documentation
    │   └── AchievementRecord/ # Achievement feature
    └── ManageCourseContent/  # Management features
```

## Component Design Patterns

### 1. Feature-Oriented Architecture

**✅ GOOD: Feature-based organization**
```
CourseContent/
├── Registration/             # Complete registration feature
│   ├── index.tsx            # Main orchestrator
│   ├── types.ts             # Feature types
│   ├── RegistrationButton.tsx
│   ├── RegistrationModal.tsx
│   ├── RegistrationStatus.tsx
│   └── hooks/
│       └── useRegistrationHandler.ts
└── AchievementRecord/        # Achievement feature
    ├── index.tsx
    ├── UploadModal.tsx
    └── hooks/
```

**❌ AVOID: Technology-based organization**
```
components/
├── buttons/
├── modals/
├── forms/
└── hooks/
```

### 2. Component Composition Patterns

#### Container/Presentational Pattern
```typescript
// Container: Handles data and logic
const CourseContent: FC<{ id: number }> = ({ id }) => {
  const { data, loading, error } = useAdminQuery(COURSE_QUERY, {
    variables: { id }
  });

  if (loading) return <CircularProgress />;
  if (error) return <ErrorMessageDialog error={error} />;

  return (
    <div>
      <CourseHeader course={data.course} />
      <CourseSessions sessions={data.sessions} />
      <Registration course={data.course} />
    </div>
  );
};

// Presentational: Pure UI components
const CourseHeader: FC<{ course: Course }> = ({ course }) => (
  <div className="course-header">
    <h1>{course.title}</h1>
    <p>{course.description}</p>
  </div>
);
```

#### Compound Component Pattern
```typescript
// Main component with sub-components
const Registration = {
  Main: RegistrationMain,
  Button: RegistrationButton,
  Modal: RegistrationModal,
  Status: RegistrationStatus,
};

// Usage
<Registration.Main course={course}>
  <Registration.Button />
  <Registration.Status />
</Registration.Main>
```

### 3. Component Interface Design

#### Props Interface Patterns
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Clear, specific interfaces
interface RegistrationProps {
  course: Course_Course_by_pk;
  courseEnrollment?: CourseWithEnrollment_Course_by_pk_CourseEnrollments;
  onRegistrationSuccess?: () => void;
}

// ✅ GOOD: Generic with constraints
interface EntityListManagerProps<TEntity, TSelectedEntity> {
  entities: TEntity[];
  selectedEntities: TSelectedEntity[];
  onSelectionChange: (entities: TSelectedEntity[]) => void;
  renderEntity: (entity: TEntity) => ReactNode;
}

// ❌ AVOID: Vague or overly generic props
interface ComponentProps {
  data: any;
  config: any;
  options?: any;
}
```

#### Component Variants
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Variant-based design
interface ButtonProps {
  variant: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'danger';
  size: 'small' | 'medium' | 'large';
  disabled?: boolean;
  children: ReactNode;
}

// ✅ GOOD: Polymorphic components
interface UserCardProps {
  user: User;
  size: 'small' | 'medium' | 'large';
  showRole?: boolean;
  className?: string;
}
```

### 4. State Management Patterns

#### Local State for UI
```typescript
const RegistrationModal: FC<Props> = ({ isOpen, onClose }) => {
  const [motivationLetter, setMotivationLetter] = useState('');
  const [isSubmitting, setIsSubmitting] = useState(false);
  
  // UI state stays local
  const handleSubmit = async () => {
    setIsSubmitting(true);
    try {
      await submitRegistration({ motivationLetter });
      onClose();
    } finally {
      setIsSubmitting(false);
    }
  };
};
```

#### Server State with GraphQL
```typescript
const CourseContent: FC<{ id: number }> = ({ id }) => {
  // Server state managed by Apollo
  const { data, loading, error } = useAdminQuery(COURSE_QUERY, {
    variables: { id },
    errorPolicy: 'all'
  });

  // Derived state
  const isEnrolled = useMemo(() => 
    data?.course?.enrollments?.some(e => e.userId === currentUserId),
    [data, currentUserId]
  );
};
```

#### Custom Hooks for Complex Logic
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Extract complex logic to custom hooks
const useRegistrationHandler = ({
  course,
  onSuccess
}: UseRegistrationHandlerProps) => {
  const [mutation] = useRoleMutation(ENROLL_MUTATION);
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false);

  const handleRegistration = useCallback(async (data: RegistrationData) => {
    setIsLoading(true);
    try {
      await mutation({ variables: { courseId: course.id, ...data } });
      onSuccess?.();
    } catch (error) {
      // Handle error
    } finally {
      setIsLoading(false);
    }
  }, [mutation, course.id, onSuccess]);

  return { handleRegistration, isLoading };
};
```

## Component Reuse Guidelines

### 1. Component Decision Matrix

| Need | Check First | Use If Available |
|------|-------------|------------------|
| **Error Display** | `ErrorMessageDialog` | ✅ Standard error dialog |
| **User Confirmation** | `QuestionConfirmationDialog` | ✅ Yes/no confirmation |
| **Custom Modal** | `BaseDialog` | ✅ Flexible dialog wrapper |
| **Toast Notification** | `NotificationSnackbar` | ✅ Temporary notifications |
| **Tag/Alias Input** | `CreatableTagSelector` | ✅ Supports creation + selection |
| **Dropdown Selection** | `DropDownSelector` | ✅ Standard dropdown with options |
| **Data Table** | `TableGrid` | ✅ Pagination, sorting, filtering |
| **Text Input** | `InputField` | ✅ Standard form input |
| **Button** | `Button` | ✅ Consistent styling |
| **User Display** | `UserCard` | ✅ User profile display |

### 2. Component Extension Patterns

#### Composition over Inheritance
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Compose existing components
const CourseRegistration: FC<Props> = ({ course }) => (
  <BaseDialog open={isOpen} onClose={onClose}>
    <InputField
      label={t('motivation_letter')}
      value={motivationLetter}
      onChange={setMotivationLetter}
    />
    <Button variant="primary" onClick={handleSubmit}>
      {t('submit_application')}
    </Button>
  </BaseDialog>
);

// ❌ AVOID: Extending components through inheritance
class CustomDialog extends BaseDialog {
  // Don't do this
}
```

#### Higher-Order Components for Cross-Cutting Concerns
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: HOC for authentication
const withAuth = <P extends object>(Component: React.ComponentType<P>) => {
  return (props: P) => {
    const { isLoggedIn } = useIsLoggedIn();
    
    if (!isLoggedIn) {
      return <LoginPrompt />;
    }
    
    return <Component {...props} />;
  };
};

// Usage
const ProtectedCourseContent = withAuth(CourseContent);
```

### 3. Component Testing Patterns

#### Component Testing Structure
```typescript
// Component.test.tsx
describe('Registration Component', () => {
  const mockCourse = { id: 1, title: 'Test Course' };
  
  it('renders registration button for eligible users', () => {
    render(<Registration course={mockCourse} />);
    expect(screen.getByText('Apply Now')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
  
  it('shows modal when button is clicked', async () => {
    render(<Registration course={mockCourse} />);
